{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1090059-dragonblooded-officer-corps","id":1090059,"title":"Dragonblooded officer corps","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-08T17:51:09-07:00","id":1090059,"title":"Dragonblooded officer corps","content":"What's the minimum unit of troops a Dragonblooded commands? I assume a scale is far, far too small for a dragonblooded to head automatically, but certainly most legion leaders will be Dragonblooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:11:03-07:00","id":1090071,"title":"","content":"That sounds about right for an entry level position for an Exalt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:12:50-07:00","id":1090073,"title":"","content":"Scales for Lookshy special forces, Talons for Realm special forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:19:08-07:00","id":1090075,"title":"","content":"A talon sounds about right so the Dragon-Blooded has mortal lieutenants under his command, but I assume it's possible for a Dragon-Blooded to command a scale under certain circumstances. For example, if a task requires five Dragon-Blooded and a talon of soldiers, which would give them a scale each, or if a manse on the Blessed Isle requires a small contingent of guards as a formality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:24:45-07:00","id":1090077,"title":"","content":"What kind of army are we talking about in the first place? Or rather, what section of the army? A legion formation, or one of the auxiliary units?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:28:27-07:00","id":1090080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1090059-dragonblooded-officer-corps?p=1090077#post1090077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of army are we talking about in the first place? Or rather, what section of the army? A legion formation, or one of the auxiliary units?</div> </div> </div> </div>Legion, specifically raised by Parsaad as opposed to a Realm-raised one (War of Independence that my solars will be dragged into. Working out numbers of troops and dragonblooded from there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T22:37:03-07:00","id":1090124,"title":"","content":"With Prasad, we don't really know: how many DB officers are there? How many soldiers? The more DBs there are, the lower-ranked some will be.<br /> <br /> Saying it's the same as the Realm's system is probably fine, but it's worth considering overall numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:17:28-07:00","id":1090221,"title":"","content":"Really, the highest ranks are usually filled by Dragon-blooded and the minimum ranks is really just the highest rank not currently occupied by a Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> One specific point of note is the Vermillion Legion. They almost always start Dragon-blooded at the lowest leadership positions, Scalelords and even Fanglords requiring the Dragon-blooded to prove themselves and develop a relationship with the troops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:25:46-07:00","id":1090227,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Prasad <i>might</i> be different... but on the other hand, it's not as if the entire Scarlet Dynasty serves in the Legions.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo if Prasad had fewer Dragon Blooded than the main Realm overall, but basically all of them could be theoretically called upon to command military forces, one could have about the same ratios of troops to commanders.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, part of making that work (and exploring an evolution in military organisation that I would find more interesting anyway) would probably need to require Prasad to not have the kind of full-time, professional armies that the Realm does. In keeping with the typical aesthetic of the Southeast, I would be inclined to go for something like the ways in which the armies of the Byzantine Empire differed from the post-Marian Roman Legion (or possibly contrast with the Realm by modelling Prasad's forces on the <i>pre</i>-Marian legions), or to go with something resembling the kinds of military organisation you got in the Islamic empires filling spaces from Asia Minor to the Indian subcontinent, which... is a bit complicated and something that I think my understanding of is currently rudimentary.<br /> <br /> \u200bOff the top of my head, I would describe it as a system kind of resembling feudal levies, except in which the regional governors responsible for raising individual forces are less aristocratic and a bit more centrally controlled (while still kind of being independent), sources of military levies tend to come from specialized military castes that often develop along regional ethnic lines, and distribution of battlefield roles tends to be concentrated and specialized in these particular regional lines. My impression of, say, Ottoman armies attacking Eastern Europe is that they had a very multi-cultural sense to them, while you've also got something that looks very different to the Medieval European knight. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:01:20-07:00","id":1090407,"title":"","content":"The concept of levies is definetly one I'm employing, particularly because I model Parsaad as a 'satrapy within satrapy'. <br /> Parsaad has client kingdoms all around it, with diverse cultures all their own. They pay tribute to Parsaad (who dutiful pays this mostly forward to the Realm). The result is that Parsaad is almost an independent state, and has a rather diverse looking millitary. Not as diverse looking as Ysyrs, maybe, with Ysyr's penchant of inventing new types of warriors, but still a strange bunch that is standardized only along the ethno-national lines. <br /> I have pages of political, religous, and millitary notes on the dreaming sea and it's three great powers, three ancient powers, and assorted smaller nations, provinces, and so on..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T08:19:42-07:00","id":1090726,"title":"","content":"I would be interested in seeing your stuff on the Dreaming Sea. Hm, the ratio of DB to Mortals is 1:5,000 to 1:10,000 in Creation (in 1e and 2e). Assuming that the numbers are preserved in 3e, that means that the DB are around 0.015% of the human population. Prasaad appears to cover around a million square miles (50% barren, 25% uncultivated, and 25% cultivated), so I would give it a population of around 12.8 million humans. If the DB to mortal population ratio is the average in Creation, Praasad would have a DB population of around 1,920 DB, making them the third largest DB population after the Realm and Lookshy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:24:36-07:00","id":1090772,"title":"","content":"At first I thought that seemed too much, but then, each Realm house has (on average) more than 1000 DBs, and Prasad has 2 ex-Realm houses. I probably would knock it down a bit (as Prasad's houses are likely smaller than the Realm's), but even then, it's still an absolute ton.<br /> <br /> And they probably should be the third biggest in Creation in terms of DBs, so this doesn't seem like a ridiculous number.<br /> <br /> But then, how many does Lookshy have? Over 2000? I thought it was less than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:42:11-07:00","id":1090783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1090059-dragonblooded-officer-corps?p=1090726#post1090726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be interested in seeing your stuff on the Dreaming Sea. Hm, the ratio of DB to Mortals is 1:5,000 to 1:10,000 in Creation (in 1e and 2e). Assuming that the numbers are preserved in 3e, that means that the DB are around 0.015% of the human population. Prasaad appears to cover around a million square miles (50% barren, 25% uncultivated, and 25% cultivated), so I would give it a population of around 12.8 million humans. If the DB to mortal population ratio is the average in Creation, Praasad would have a DB population of around 1,920 DB, making them the third largest DB population after the Realm and Lookshy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRatios like that should always take into consideration that demographics aren't going to be distributed evenly, especially in cases where there are cultural incentives to concentrate.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor instance, the Realm makes a policy of absorbing as many Dragon Blooded from the Threshold as it can, which will make the number in residence there lower than one might expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:45:42-07:00","id":1090784,"title":"","content":"Lookshy has 300,000 residents at a DB ratio of 1:100 in 1e and 2e, so they have around 3,000 DB (probably equally divided between natives and immigrants). Lookshy offers immigrant DBs a lot of advantages (Charm and Sorcery training, access to cool artifacts, lots of DBs of the opposite sex to procreate with, etc). I would take joining Lookshy over being a Lost Egg in the Realm any day of the week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T11:24:12-07:00","id":1090798,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay. 1500 doesn't seem so unreasonable for Prasad then. Together with Lookshy, it's less than a quarter of the DBs in the world.<br /> <br /> (1500 DBs is still an absolute<i> ton</i>, of course)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1090059-dragonblooded-officer-corps?p=1090783#post1090783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bRatios like that should always take into consideration that demographics aren't going to be distributed evenly, especially in cases where there are cultural incentives to concentrate.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor instance, the Realm makes a policy of absorbing as many Dragon Blooded from the Threshold as it can, which will make the number in residence there lower than one might expect.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but due to the distance, I imagine most DBs in the south-east will join Prasad. So Prasad's not only going to have ones born in Prasad, but also ones born all around the Dreaming Sea. Not all of course, but most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T11:40:10-07:00","id":1090807,"title":"","content":"With the proportion of DBs averaging 0.015% and the population of Creation being around 500 million humans (5% of the High First Age population of 10 billion humans), I put the DB population in Creation at 75,000 in my games. The Realm, with a DB proportion of 0.02% due to aggressive recruiting and a human population of 125 million, would have 25,000 DBs, around a third of the DBs in Creation. Lookshy would have 4% and Prasaad would have 3% of the DBs in Creation respectively. Outside of those three population centers, which account for 40% of the DBs, the DB population tends to be more distributed (more isolated Sorceresses than Company of Heroes) though the chaos of the Time of Timult may change that distribution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T12:53:48-07:00","id":1090826,"title":"","content":"The actual numbers of Dragon-Bloods vary with the telling. I have always assumed 10-15 thousand Dragon-Bloods of the Blessed Isle (including the Scarlet Dynasty and assorted others), one thousand in Lookshy and many other Outcaste groups ranging from individuals and small families to a few hundred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T13:39:46-07:00","id":1090848,"title":"","content":"It is what ever makes sense for your game. That said, a fang of 5 soldiers would be lead by a Sergeant or Corporal, who would probably be mortal or rarely a Lost Egg. At higher levels there would still be a NCO aka Sergeant at each level managing the personnel. The highest would be the Sergeant Major like rank who has the responsibility of overseeing exexution of punishment and upholding of standards. In the real world the division of ranks amongst the non officers was Private, Corporal, Sergeant, Sergeant Major and Quarter Master. <br /> Corporal held the responsibility of maintaing the discipline in his area of responsibility and that meant carrying out punishments as issued from above. They were the ones that whipped the soldier or anyother punishment hence the term corporal punishment.<br /> Sergeants took the orders from the officers and personally lead the soldiers to complete thier objective. <br /> Over all of these Sergeants was the Sergeant Major, he was attached to the commander and played the role of the &quot;bad guy&quot; essentially enforcing uniform standards and training of the masses.<br /> The Quarter Master was a non officer who over saw distribution of supplies to the soldiers as well as sleeping arrangements for the unit. Essentially these positions were to over see the minutia of managing the military to allow the officers to focus on the big picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T13:53:19-07:00","id":1090853,"title":"","content":"I imagine that many Threshold militaries would have new Outcastes leading a Talon equivalent of infantry under the guidance of a Master Sergent equivalent (an experienced Heroic Mortal) for the first few years. After they have gained some experience, the Outcaste would rise up through the ranks until they became a General (reporting directly to their Queen). With War Charms, the difference between defeat and victory might be dependent on the number of Outcaste officers that a Threshold army attracts and keeps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:46:05-07:00","id":1090876,"title":"","content":"TBH, I don't think most threshold states would really have any standardised system for integrating Dragonblood within their militaries. Prasad and Lookshy sure, and a few other places like Cherak.<br /> <br /> But other than that, it's rare enough that it's going to depend on whoever's in charge: they might demand the outcaste join normally and work their way up, put them straight into an officer's rank, or something else entirely like making them champion duelist. It's going to depend a lot on the culture, who the outcaste is (I mean, do they have war charms? Do they have sorcery? Are they a master of archery, or sail, or ride? They could be quite varied), how they turned up, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:49:41-07:00","id":1090878,"title":"","content":"For one thing, most of the Threshold is not allowed to form a military by the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:50:52-07:00","id":1090899,"title":"","content":"Y'all gotta remember just who you're talking to, here\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/875408-huh-less-was-more?p=876783#post876783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereal have always been unimportant in my games, primarily because my players loved being DBs. When given a choice between playing a hunted supernatural who will inevitably become corrupt and mad and playing an accepted demigod that <b>every woman wants to bang on the chance that their children will Exalt</b>, my players tended to always choose the latter (though I did let some of my female players play as secret Lunar Exalted in a DB campaign, which was really fun).</div> </div> </div> </div>His view of Creation is a bit\u2026 unusual. [/understatement]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-10-2017, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:20:28-07:00","id":1095435,"title":"","content":"From what I remember from the previous additions and the Realm legions, everything Dragon sized (500 dudes) was always DB, Wings sized (250 dudes) was almost always DB but exceptional mortals could get up that high and sometimes numbers of DB would mean that there could be some gaps. Talons are mostly staffed by mortals, with the DB at that level being inexperienced or were there because the Legion actually had enough DB to staff everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}